{{! bootstrap-version-row-dataset-guard: eager creation of a version row at seq 0 with no
    head (guide §10.1, §14.2), before the first write to it. Guards on the dataset epoch, so a writer started under an older epoch cannot create a row after a bump.
    Emitted for every append stream, and for every aggregate declared
    dal:firstWrite dal:PreCreatedRow, which gets this operation instead of
    create-if-absent. Run it when the aggregate or stream id is allocated.
    Bind $target to the same IRI later bound as $root (CAS, tombstone) or
    $stream (append). The first CAS then expects seq 0 and finds no head.
    A lazy initialisation inside the first write would reintroduce the
    first-write race. Idempotent: a no-op if the row exists.
    Note for template authors: never put a Mustache tag inside this
    comment block. Chevron's comment parser ends at the first closing
    double-brace it sees, which silently truncates the comment. }}
PREFIX pat: <https://example.org/lattice/patterns#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

INSERT {
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} { $target a pat:VersionRow ; pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq "0"^^xsd:long }
}
WHERE {
  GRAPH {{{datasetGraph}}} { {{{datasetNode}}} pat:epoch $epoch }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} { $target pat:seq ?any } }
}
